course: dictionary
lesson: 7841
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, shows you which meaning the writer chose. «A bike is locked by its frame and a wheel to a fixed bike rack, because unlocked bikes are stolen.» Here a rack is a frame you can lock a bike to, so it is a thing you can touch and use.
explain: Rack can also be a verb, an action word. To rack your brains is to think very hard to remember or solve something. Rack up means to collect or gain a lot, like points in a game. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or is it something someone is doing?
explain: «Clothes on a drying rack dry because the water slowly evaporates into the air; wind and warmth make it faster.» The clues are drying, dry and wind, so the rack is the frame that holds wet clothes while they dry. When you are unsure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A rack is a frame or shelf with bars, hooks or spaces for holding things.
fact: Examples of racks are a coat rack, a bike rack, a toast rack and a cooling rack.
fact: «Rack your brains» means to think very hard to remember or solve something.
fact: «Rack up» means to collect or gain a lot, like points.
fact: «Off the rack» describes clothes that are already made in sizes, not made especially for one person.
exercise: «A bike is locked to a fixed bike rack, because unlocked bikes are stolen.» What is a bike rack? | A lock made of metal chain | A cycle path along the road | *A frame with bars or spaces for holding bikes | A fast bike with many gears
exercise: Sam had to rack his brains to remember the password. What does rack his brains mean? | To hang his coat up | To drop his ideas on the floor | *To think very hard | To shake his head sadly
exercise: «Maya racked up 50 points in the game.» What does racked up mean? | To drop points quickly | To clean up a mess | *To collect or gain a lot | To hang up on a hook
test: «Clothes on a drying rack dry faster on a windy day.» What makes clothes dry faster? | Darkness and cold | *Wind and warmth, which make the water evaporate faster | Being folded up tight | Rain falling on them
test: Which phrase means to think very hard to solve something? | Off the rack | Cooling rack | Bike rack | *Rack your brains
exam: Which example uses rack as a verb, an action word? | *Rack up points | Coat rack | Bike rack | Cooling rack
